# Nucleus — Code Standards

## The Prime Directive
Every file you write must be production-ready. No TODOs left in code, no placeholder logic, no "this will do for now." If you're not sure how to implement something properly, say so instead of writing bad code.

## TypeScript
```ts
// NEVER use any
const data: any = ...  // ❌

// ALWAYS define proper types
interface NoteCardProps {
  note: Note
  onDelete: (id: string) => void
}
```

Always import types with `import type { }` when it's a type-only import.

## Error Handling

### Server actions — always return typed results
```ts
// Return shape must always be consistent
return { data: result }   // success
return { error: 'message' }  // failure — never throw, always return

// Never do this in a server action
throw new Error('something failed')
```

### Client components — always handle loading and error states
```tsx
const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false)
const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null)

// Always show feedback to user
if (error) return <p className="text-red-400 text-sm">{error}</p>
```

### Always use sonner for user-facing feedback
```ts
import { toast } from 'sonner'

toast.success('Note created')
toast.error('Failed to create note')
```

## Component Structure
```tsx
// 1. Imports (external → internal → types)
// 2. Types/interfaces
// 3. Component function
// 4. Hooks at top
// 5. Derived state
// 6. Handlers
// 7. Return JSX

'use client'

import { useState } from 'react'
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { createNote } from '../actions/notes.actions'
import type { Note } from '../types'

interface Props {
  clusterId: string | null
}

export function CreateNoteButton({ clusterId }: Props) {
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false)

  async function handleCreate() {
    setIsLoading(true)
    const result = await createNote({ clusterId, title: 'Untitled' })
    if (result.error) toast.error(result.error)
    setIsLoading(false)
  }

  return (
    <Button onClick={handleCreate} disabled={isLoading}>
      {isLoading ? 'Creating...' : 'New Note'}
    </Button>
  )
}
```

## What Never To Do
- Never use `console.log` — use `console.error` only for actual errors
- Never leave commented-out code blocks
- Never use `!important` in styles
- Never use inline styles — Tailwind classes only
- Never install new npm packages — ask first
- Never import from `@supabase/supabase-js` directly
- Never add Framer Motion or any animation library
- Never use `as any` TypeScript cast — find the proper type
- Never hardcode user IDs, API keys, or secrets
- Never fetch data client-side when it can be done server-side
- Never duplicate logic that already exists in `lib/`

## File Naming
```
components → kebab-case.tsx         (note-card.tsx)
actions    → kebab-case.actions.ts  (notes.actions.ts)
types      → index.ts inside types/ folder
hooks      → use-kebab-case.ts      (use-notes.ts)
```

## Surgical Edits Only
When asked to fix or modify something:
- Change ONLY what is needed
- Do not refactor unrelated code
- Do not rename variables that aren't part of the fix
- Do not add new features while fixing a bug
- Do not rewrite a whole file when one function needs changing

## Prompt Cache Everything
Any Anthropic API call system prompt must have `cache_control: { type: 'ephemeral' }` on the system message and the `anthropic-beta: 'prompt-caching-2024-07-31'` header. This is non-negotiable — it directly affects cost.

## Security Checklist (Run Through This For Every API Route)
- [ ] Is `supabase.auth.getUser()` called before anything else?
- [ ] Is `requirePro()` called if this is an AI route?
- [ ] Are all database queries filtered by `user_id`?
- [ ] Is the response body validated before use?
- [ ] Are error messages generic to the client (no internal details leaked)?
- [ ] Is the HTTP status code correct (401/403/422/500)?
